<div class="wrap page-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">Primary · 5 to 11 years</p>
  <h1>Cambridge in the morning, <span class="mark">mud by lunchtime</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">Primary follows the Cambridge International curriculum for English, Maths, and Science, taught by qualified teachers in classes of {{ site.classCap }} or fewer. Then the day opens up: sport, cooking, art, technology.</p>
</div>

<section class="band--paper">
  <div class="wrap two">
    <div>
      <h2>The academic core</h2>
      <p><strong>English</strong> is reading real books, writing things people will read, and talking. A lot of talking. <strong>Maths</strong> starts with objects and patterns and works up to the abstract. <strong>Science</strong> is experiments first, explanations second.</p>
      <p>The Cambridge Primary framework means your child's progress is measured against a standard schools recognise anywhere, and moving to another school later is straightforward.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="photo photo--blob" data-caption="photo: a science experiment in a Year 2 or 3 class"></div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set riverColor = "var(--sand)" %}{% include "partials/river.njk" %}

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>The rest of the day</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>PE, every day</h3><p>Structured sport, calisthenics, and free play, in rotation. The aim is that every child finds something physical they like enough to keep doing.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Vocational classes</h3><p>Subjects rotate each year so children meet a range of skills. This year: technology, fashion and design, and art, taught by specialists. Assessed by making things, not by tests.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Year 6 Checkpoint</h3><p>Optional. A Cambridge diagnostic test in English, Maths, and Science at the end of Primary. It gives a clear picture of strengths and gaps, and practice at sitting a formal exam.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Reports and meetings</h3><p>Written progress reports and two parent and teacher meetings a year, in October and March. In between, just ask.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

